{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-340871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=-2{x}^{3}+3x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-2(-x)^{3}+3(-x)) \\\\  & =-(2{x}^{3}-3x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}+3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-340871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{x}^{3}+3x"] ["math" "-2{x}^{3}-3x"] ["math" "-2|x{|}^{3}-3|x|"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-3x"] ["math" "|2{x}^{3}-3x|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{x}^{3}+3x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=3{x}^{2}-2x$ for $x\\in [0,5),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-5,5).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-5,0)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,5),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,5), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-5,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-5,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(3(-x)^{2}-2(-x)) \\\\  & =-(3{x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-340866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3{x}^{2}+2x"] ["math" "-3{x}^{2}-2x"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}-2x"] ["math" "3|x{|}^{2}+2|x|"] ["math" "|-3{x}^{2}+2x|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3{x}^{2}-2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}-3x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-4(-x)^{2}-3(-x)) \\\\  & =-(-4{x}^{2}+3x) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-340868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{x}^{2}-3x"] ["math" "-4|x{|}^{2}+3|x|"] ["math" "4{x}^{2}+3x"] ["math" "4{x}^{2}-3x"] ["math" "|4{x}^{2}+3x|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{x}^{2}-3x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-2x$ for $x\\in [0,10),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-10,10).$ What is the value of $f(-6)?$\n\n$f(-6)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,10),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,10), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-10,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-10,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}-2(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-6) & =-(-6)^{2}-2(-6)=-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-341406" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341406" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=-{x}^{2}+5x$ for $x\\in [0,8),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-8,8).$ What is the value of $f(-3)?$\n\n$f(-3)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,8),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,8), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-8,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-8,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-(-x)^{2}+5(-x)) \\\\  & =-(-{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{2}+5(-3)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-341210" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341210" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${b}_{n}.$\n$\\,{b}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{10}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-340926" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340926" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{10(1+(-1)^{n})}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{10(1-(-1)^{n})}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{5(1-(-1)^{n})}{n}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340926" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{10}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{10(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}"] ["math" "\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{2(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-340629" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-2x+3$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${b}_{n}.$$\\,{b}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-2x+3$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-2x+3\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[(-2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{2}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-2\\pi +3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{2}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-2\\pi +3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-3+\\frac{2}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-2\\pi +3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-2\\pi +3)(-1)^{n}-3)=\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(2\\pi -3)+3).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-341381" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" 