e_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=-3x+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-3x+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-3x+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-3x+2\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[(-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{3}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{3}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2+\\frac{3}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)(-1)^{n}-2)=\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2).\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "911a6bf954e6ecbfb02c974997c9f41acf238a8364a0eab4eeb2d4e437c8472b"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi +2)-2)"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)"] ["math" "\\frac{3(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "q-341336" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cc7a32b7520907757691870883adc81a25b4fefa0fe4b0d53c5a3151b1878d9"} {"question" "e-21809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=x^2+10x$ for $x\\in[0,6),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x \\in (-6,6).$ What is the value of $f(-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/example-21809.json" "file_sha256" "bb87462989c4539585e6988125b443b0ce6847f72dc19c8ebd82bcd57f9545a2"} {"question" "e-21809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in[0,6),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/assets/3d7a4a25652434612765ebef26c7c0956342611968008bc4908a4865297e047d.png)\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in(-6,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}+10(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-10x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =-(-1)^{2}+10(-1)=-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/example-21809.json" "file_sha256" "bb87462989c4539585e6988125b443b0ce6847f72dc19c8ebd82bcd57f9545a2"} {"question" "e-21810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=4x$ for $x\\in[0,\\pi).$ Find the missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/assets/20ec903a94cb720f0d2c50b427409e36705af1f9f226b5c6fb11f93f92f0dd49.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/example-21810.json" "file_sha256" "4d8def941babd89be3c799389b41fedc6f443a5ba88268768b185254509592c9"} {"question" "e-21810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\nb_n=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi f(x)\\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=4x$ for $x \\in (0,\\pi).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nb_n = \\dfrac{8}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi x \\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\cos(n\\pi)=(-1)^n,$ we have\n\n$$\nb_n = -\\dfrac{8(-1)^n}{n}=\\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n} \\cdot \\sin(nx).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/example-21810.json" "file_sha256" "4d8def941babd89be3c799389b41fedc6f443a5ba88268768b185254509592c9"}] "usage" {"e-21809" [] "e-21810" [] "q-340629" []} "basis" 2298 "retractions" [[17592186167221 :question/problem "Let $F(x) =-5x$ for $[MATH: x ∈ [0, π).]$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2π$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.$(2(-1)^{n})/(n)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}"] [17592186166499 :question/problem "Let $F(x)=x^2+10x$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,6),]$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x \\in (-6,6)$. What is the value of $f(-1)$?"] [17592186166499 :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $[MATH: x\\in[0,6),]$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n$[MATH: {F(x), \\mid x ∈ [0, 6),; - F(-x), \\mid x ∈ (-6, 0).]$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in(-6,0)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= -F(-x) \\\\\n&= - ((-x)^{2} + 10(-x)) \\\\\n&= - (x^{2} - 10x) \\\\\n&=-x^{2} + 10x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= - (-1)^{2} + 10(-1) =-11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186166500 :question/problem "Let $F(x)=4x$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,\\pi).]$ Find the missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$AAAAA_{A}^{A}$"] [17592186166500 :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\nb_n=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi f(x)\\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nf(x)=4x\n$$\n\nfor $x \\in (0,\\pi)$. So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nb_n = \\dfrac{8}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi x \\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & ⇒u^{′} = 1 \\\\ v^{′} = \\sin (nx) & ⇒v =-\\frac{1}{n}\\cos (nx)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb_{n} &= \\left.\\frac{8}{π}(uv\\right|_{0}^{π} - \\int_{0}^{π}vu^{′}dx) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{π}(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\cos (nx)]_{0}^{π} + \\frac{1}{n}\\int_{0}^{π}\\cos (nx)dx) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{8}{nπ}((π \\cdot \\cos (nπ) - 0 \\cdot \\cos (0)) - \\frac{1}{n}[\\sin (nx)]_{0}^{π}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{8}{nπ}(π\\cos (nπ) - \\frac{1}{n}(\\sin (nπ) - \\sin (0))) \\\\\n&= - (8\\cos (nπ))/(n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n\\cos(n\\pi)=(-1)^n\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\nb_n = -\\dfrac{8(-1)^n}{n}=\\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n}\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n} \\cdot \\sin(nx)\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186164888 17592186164889 17592186164890 17592186164891 17592186164893 17592186164894 17592186164895 17592186164896] "immutable_fields" [[17592186164887 :answer-field/correct] [17592186164887 :answer-field/id] [17592186164887 :answer-field/key] [17592186164887 :answer-field/type] [17592186164892 :answer-field/correct] [17592186164892 :answer-field/id] [17592186164892 :answer-field/key] [17592186164892 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
